                <pb facs="0784" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.91/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cheat Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-18T19:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1919, 7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            August 19, 2.22 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2831. At interview this afternoon for that purpose Curzon states that French
                    sentiment seems hostile to Anglo-Persian agreement and <pb facs="0785" n="700"
                        xml:id="pg700"/> French Minister at Teheran disposed to foment
                    dissatisfaction, in which he hopes for assistance of American Minister. Requests
                    mat latter be put on guard and asked to preserve friendly attitude.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
